Description: Preserve the inputPush ownership result when the parser has halted
 A successfully pushed input belongs to the parser even if it has reached EOF.
 Keep the existing early exit and return the actual stack result. This
 backport changes no public declarations.
Origin: vendor, adapted from the remediation described in https://errata.tuxcare.com/els_os/debian10els/CLSA-2026-1789202279.html
Bug-Debian: https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-6653
Forwarded: not-needed
--- a/parser.c
+++ b/parser.c
@@ -2313,7 +2313,7 @@ xmlPushInput(xmlParserCtxtPtr ctxt, xmlParserInputPtr input) {
     }
     ret = inputPush(ctxt, input);
     if (ctxt->instate == XML_PARSER_EOF)
-        return(-1);
+        return(ret);
     GROW;
     return(ret);
 }
